## Job catalog ingest

Added 2026-10-24, after the catalog had been stale for 54 days.

The ~11k job pages are the only part of the site with organic reach: sitemapped, with
`JobPosting` JSON-LD, which is the entry ticket to Google Jobs. `README.md` used to say
the catalog refreshed every 6 hours via the `jobs-ingest` CronJob in `k8s/`. **It never
did** — those manifests are not applied (Offerfy is not a k8s Deployment, hard rule 5),
and nothing else scheduled it. The last pass ran **2026-09-01**. `validThrough` is
`last_seen_at + 30 days`, so on **2026-10-01** the entire catalog expired at once and
the sitemap advertised 11k expired postings for three weeks. Nothing noticed: there is
no analytics and no Search Console on this site, and the ingest exited 0 even when
every source failed.

It is a **user** unit on purpose. Agent sessions have no passwordless sudo, and a user
timer needs none. It requires lingering, enabled 2026-10-24:

```bash
loginctl show-user ruby0322 --property=Linger      # must be Linger=yes
```

`loginctl enable-linger ruby0322` was accepted **without a password** (polkit allows
self-linger here), which is also the trick for any future unattended user unit.

Install or refresh after editing `ops/systemd/offerfy-ingest.*` — no sudo:

```bash
mkdir -p ~/.config/systemd/user
cp /home/ruby0322/offerfy/ops/systemd/offerfy-ingest.{service,timer} ~/.config/systemd/user/
systemctl --user daemon-reload
systemctl --user enable --now offerfy-ingest.timer
```

Operate it:

```bash
systemctl --user list-timers offerfy-ingest.timer --no-pager   # NEXT / LAST / PASSED
systemctl --user start offerfy-ingest.service                  # one pass; minutes, blocks
journalctl --user -u offerfy-ingest.service -n 40 --no-pager
```

The unit reads `EnvironmentFile=/home/ruby0322/offerfy/.env.production` (so
`DATABASE_URL` → `127.0.0.1:5433`) and runs `.venv/bin/python -m app.jobs.ingest_catalog`
with cwd `apps/backend`. It does **not** order itself after Postgres — a user manager
cannot order against system or docker units. That is deliberate and safe: a pass that
starts before Postgres is up fails, exits non-zero, and `Persistent=true` means the next
slot picks it up.

### Two guards — do not remove without replacing

1. **Non-zero exit when a pass refreshed nothing.** `app.jobs.ingest_catalog` aggregates
   per-source results and returns 1 if every source failed or none returned a job, so a
   stalled catalog surfaces as a **failed unit**. One dead board among many still exits
   0, because the catalog did get refreshed. Check `journalctl` for `sources_ok=… 
   sources_failed=… upserted=…`.
2. **Staleness is derived from `last_seen_at`, never from `is_active` alone.**
   `is_active` only flips when an ingest run observes a posting gone, so a dead ingest
   leaves every row active indefinitely while its markup expires underneath it.
   `JOB_FRESHNESS_DAYS = 30` exists in **two** places that must stay in step:
   `apps/frontend/lib/seo.ts` (noindex + drop JSON-LD past the window; also the source
   of `validThrough`) and `apps/backend/app/routers/jobs.py` (drop those rows from
   `/v1/jobs/sitemap`). A dead ingest now degrades to honest noindex instead of serving
   expired postings.

### Still open

Nothing pages anyone when the unit fails — `systemctl --user list-timers` and the
`job_ingest_runs` table are the only signals. And with no analytics or Search Console
anywhere on the site, "is Google crawling the job pages" remains unanswerable from here.

