## Firewall (minikube → host :3200)

UFW default **INPUT/FORWARD DROP**. Minikube pods cannot reach host `:3200` unless allowed. Symptom: public HTTPS **504**.

Required (not guaranteed persistent across reboot / `ufw reload`):

```bash
sudo ufw allow from 192.168.49.0/24 to any port 3200 proto tcp
# optional if you ever point Ingress at next dev:
sudo ufw allow from 192.168.49.0/24 to any port 3100 proto tcp
```

Equivalent iptables: `ACCEPT` from `192.168.49.0/24` to tcp **3200**.

Quick check from cluster:

```bash
kubectl -n offerfy-native-tmp run curlcheck --rm -i --restart=Never --image=curlimages/curl:8.5.0 \
  -- curl -sS -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' --max-time 8 http://192.168.49.1:3200/
```

Expect `200`. If it hangs on image pull, wait; do not leave the pod.

