## Security posture (audit 2026-10-22)

Triggered by NTU CERT notice **NISAC-110-202610-00000035** (alleged intrusion
2026-07-26..28 from `159.223.38[.]244`). No evidence of *that* intrusion was found, but
the audit surfaced an unrelated live exposure. See also `/root/incident-NISAC-202610/`.

### Fixed: object store was world-open

`seaweedfs-s3` published `0.0.0.0:8334` **and** SeaweedFS S3 runs with no `-s3.config`,
so it performed **no authentication at all**. Anonymous `ListAllMyBuckets`,
`ListBucket`, `GetObject`, `PutObject` and `CreateBucket` all succeeded from the public
IP. `offerfy-private` holds real user uploads. Postgres `5433` was published the same way.

Both are now `127.0.0.1:`-bound (hard rule 9). **Binding is the only control in place —
there is still no S3 authentication.** Anything that can reach the host can read every
bucket.

