### Tests write to the production bucket

`apps/backend/tests/conftest.py` pins `DATABASE_URL` to in-memory SQLite and `APP_ENV` to
`development`, but **never overrides `S3_ENDPOINT` / `S3_BUCKET`**, so pydantic falls
through to repo-root `.env` and every `pytest` run PUTs fixtures into live
`offerfy-private`. Confirmed: a 2026-10-22 run added 27 objects.

Of 473 objects, **465 are test fixtures** (`notes.txt` x325+, `SWE_Resume.pdf` x46,
`Ada Lovelace CV.pdf` x21, `jd.txt` x40). Write bursts: 2026-08-26 (114), 08-27 (187),
09-01 (27), 09-17 (18), 10-09 (72), 10-22 (45). Nothing in the app ever *reads* these
back (see below), so they are pure liability.

Fix before running the suite again:

```python
