## Troubleshooting

| Symptom | Cause | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| HTTPS 404 / wrong cert | Host not on Ingress, or DNS not to abbey | Add host + TLS; `dig +short <host> A` = `140.112.106.204` |
| ACME pending `no such host` inside cluster | CoreDNS NXDOMAIN cache | Restart `kube-system` `coredns`; wait; grey-cloud DNS |
| ACME pending, DNS OK | Orange cloud, or `:80` bridge down | Grey cloud; `docker ps` bridge; HTTP-01 on `:80` |
| HTTPS 504 | minikube cannot reach `192.168.49.1:3200` | UFW/iptables allow `192.168.49.0/24` → 3200; `systemctl status offerfy-web` |
| Google login `redirect_uri` is `127.0.0.1` | Public `.next` rewrite baked dest `:8002` | `npm run build:public`; confirm routes-manifest `:8001`; restart `offerfy-web`. Do not "fix" by editing live `GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI` on dest `.env` |
| HTML 200, `/api` 500 | uvicorn `:8001` down | `sudo systemctl restart offerfy-api`; Next log shows `ECONNREFUSED ... port: 8001` |
| After reboot, public dead | minikube / pd-care bridge / UFW / compose, not Offerfy units | `systemctl status offerfy-api offerfy-web`; start minikube + pd-care bridge + compose infra; re-check UFW |
| pd-care HTTPS/ACME broken | Something else bound `:80`/`:443` | Stop it; restore pd-care ingress-bridge |
| Resume upload returns 5xx, `S3 put_object failed` in journal | S3 unreachable or credentials wrong. Since 2026-10-22 this fails loudly instead of losing the file silently | `curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}' http://127.0.0.1:8334/` ; `docker compose ps seaweedfs-s3` ; check `S3_*` in `.env.production` |
| `pytest` adds objects to `offerfy-private` | `conftest.py` does not override `S3_ENDPOINT`/`S3_BUCKET` | See *Security posture → Tests write to the production bucket* |

